#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Combine every broker's holdings from Redis into one holdings document, the way the REST API's `/api/portfolio/holdings`
answers, and write it to the Redis key `unified:portfolio:holdings` every minute.

    bin/unified/portfolio/holdings
    redis-cli GET unified:portfolio:holdings

Nothing here calls a broker. Each broker's holdings are already kept in Redis by `bin/<broker>/portfolio/holdings`, as
`{"timestamp", "status", "code", "data"}` under `<broker>:portfolio:holdings`, the instruments by
`bin/unified/instruments/map`, and live prices by `bin/unified/instruments/websocket_quotes` in `unified:quotes:live`, so this reads those and
interprets them.

**The document** has the REST API's shape:

    {"holdings": [...], "summary": {"holdings_count", "total_investment", "total_current_value", "total_unrealized_pnl"},
     "brokers": [...], "as_of": ...}

A holding is `instrument_id`, `isin`, `symbol`, `exchange`, `segment`, `quantity`, `average_price`, `invested_value`,
`last_price`, `current_value`, `pnl` (`unrealized`, `day_change`, `day_change_percentage`) and `collateral_quantity`,
sorted by symbol.

**Each broker's holding** is read like this. Quantity is everything held, across
the broker's buckets, and invested value each bucket at its own average price:

| broker | stored rows | token, exchange | quantity, invested at | pledged | prices |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| zerodha | `data` | `instrument_token`, `exchange` | `quantity` + `t1_quantity` at `average_price`, plus `mtf.quantity` at `mtf.average_price` | `collateral_quantity` | `last_price`, `close_price` |
| dhan | `data` (DH-1111 stored as `[]`) | `securityId`, `exchange` | `totalQty` at `avgCostPrice` | `collateralQty` | `lastTradedPrice` |
| flattrade, shoonya | `data` | first `exch_tsym` listing's `token`, `exch` | `holdqty` + `npoadqty` + `npoadt1qty` at `upldprc` | `colqty` | `c` as close |
| fyers | `data.holdings` | `fyToken`, the symbol's prefix | `quantity` + `qty_t1` at `costPrice` | `collateralQuantity` | `ltp` |
| groww | `data.holdings` | no token, first `tradable_exchanges` | `quantity` at `average_price` | `pledge_quantity` | none |
| indmoney | `data` | `security_id`, NSE | `total_qty` at `avg_price` | `used_qty` | none |
| kotak | `data` | `exchangeIdentifier`, `exchangeSegment` | `quantity` at `averagePrice` | none | `closingPrice` as close |
| stoxkart | `data` | `nse_token` or `bse_token`, whichever `exchange` names, else the other | `quantity` at `average_price` | `collateral_quantity` | `last_trade_price` |
| wisdom_capital | `data.RMSHoldings.Holdings`, keyed by ISIN | NSE instrument id, else BSE's | `HoldingQuantity` at `BuyAvgPrice` | `CollateralQuantity` or `PledgeQuantity` | none |

A missing or non-numeric quantity reads as zero; a missing or zero price stays unknown.

**Resolving** uses the Redis cache. A holding's token is looked up in
`unified:broker_tokens` among the cash segments - equities, exchange traded funds, investment trusts, mutual funds,
fixed income, uncategorised - on the exchange the broker names, or on NSE then BSE when it names none, and several
candidates are taken in that segment order. Groww sends no token, so a Groww holding is looked up by its symbol in
`unified:instrument_symbols` over the same segments. A holding nothing resolves keeps the broker's symbol and no id.

**Merging** takes brokers in name order, and two holdings are one row when they share an ISIN or an
instrument id, so Kotak, which sends no ISIN, joins the row another broker's ISIN started once its token resolves.
Quantities, invested values and pledged quantities add up, the row keeps the first instrument it resolved to, and a
price from any broker is the instrument's, the latest one read winning.

**Pricing.** A resolved holding is priced by its instrument's live quote in `unified:quotes:live`,
kept by `bin/unified/instruments/websocket_quotes`: the quote's `last_price`, and its `previous_close` for the day change, or a broker's previous
close when the quote has none. A quote is used by the rule the REST API's quote service serves its cache by - not when it
is marked `stale`, and only when it was received in the last five minutes or the instrument's trading window has closed
since and not reopened, judged against the exchanges' calendars. Nothing here asks a broker for a quote, so a holding
whose quote is not usable - and one with no instrument or no quote - is priced by the last price a broker sent and its
previous close, or failing a last price by the previous close, with no day change.
Groww, INDmoney and Wisdom Capital send neither, so a holding only they carry and with no usable quote has no `last_price`, `current_value`, `unrealized` or day change.

`brokers` says, for each broker, how its stored holdings were read: `ok`, `stale` (stored more than three minutes ago -
its script may have stopped; its holdings are still included), `missing` (no key) or `unreadable`, with `as_of`, when
its script stored them.

Written with SET every minute. Runs until Ctrl+C or SIGTERM; a Redis that cannot be reached is logged and tried again.
Reads only - it places no orders.
"""

